  "Description": {
    "Cost": 1030937,
    "UIName": "Clint",
    "Id": "chassisdef_clint_CLNT-3-4T",
    "Name": "Clint",
    "Details": "The latest iteration of the Clint is a sensible upgrade rather than a revolution. It shares many components with the Cadaver. This is a great advantage in the Periphery, where new components are perpetually  scarce, especially for a volatile 'Mech like the Clint. The upgrade removed many of its troublesome features, to the joy of technicians. Its weapons array benefited from concurrent developments. This includes X-pulse technology, first used by the Taurians on the Brahma, which had since reached maturity for full-scale production. The new Clint's reflective armor remains a gamble that could possibly undo its other logistical  advantages\n\n<b><color=#e62e00>Quirk: Variable Range Targeting</color></b>\n\n<b><color=#e62e00>Drop Cost Multiplier: 1.02</color></b>\n\n<color=#FFEF00>Arm Actuator Limit: Right Lower</color>",
    "Icon": "Clint"
  },
  "VariantName": "CLNT-3-4T",
  "ChassisTags": {
    "items": [
      "ArmLimitLowerRight",
      "OneHanded"
    ]
  },
  "StockRole": "Sniper & Light Brawler",
  "YangsThoughts": "The Clint was primarily designed as a cheap recon unit, with the capabilities of a well-armed, low-end medium weight 'Mech, and in this regard it served well. With a top speed of 97.2 km/h and a jumping capability of one hundred and eighty meters, the Clint can easily keep up with other recon elements and maneuver through mountainous or urban terrain. Produced by the Taurian Concordat at the outbreak of the Jihad, the 3-3T modifies the original 2-3T. It adds Ferro-Fibrous armor to the design and swaps out the AC/5 with a Light AC/5, presumably supplied to them by the Word of Blake. This lighter weapon makes room for the inclusion of CASE and two tons of ammunition, ensuring it is able to carry various types of munitions.",
